--- README.md ---
# admin-web: dynamic forms

Every form in the admin app is drawn from a JSON field config.

- `GET /api/forms/{formId}` returns the form's config (shape in `src/forms/types.ts`).
- `DynamicForm` loads the config, sets each field's starting value from its
  `defaultValue`, and renders one `FieldInput` per field.
- On submit, `validate` runs, then the values are sent as JSON with
  `POST <submitUrl>`.

Configs are owned by the config service. Product admins edit them there and the
change is live at once; the frontend is not redeployed. 23 forms are served this
way.

## Checks

Every pull request runs `npm run typecheck` (`tsc --noEmit`, strict) and
`npm test`. TypeScript 7.0.2, React 19.3.

